Below is a **step‑by‑step playbook** you can follow to build a modern, production‑ready frontend for an e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole stack – from design to deployment – and give you concrete code snippets, folder layouts, and tooling recommendations.  
Feel free to skip sections that already fit your workflow or swap out libraries that you prefer.

---

## 1.  Planning & Design

| What to do | Why it matters |
|------------|----------------|
| **Define core user flows** – product list → product detail → cart → checkout → order confirmation | Keeps the UI focused on the most valuable actions |
| **Sketch wireframes** (Figma, Sketch, Adobe XD) | Visualise layout, spacing, and interactions before coding |
| **Create a design system** – colors, typography, spacing, reusable components | Consistency, faster hand‑off, easier maintenance |
| **Accessibility audit** (WCAG 2.1 AA) | Legal compliance & better UX |
| **SEO checklist** – meta tags, structured data, sitemap | Higher discoverability |

> **Tip:** Keep a living “product backlog” of UI/UX improvements; treat the frontend as a product in its own right.

---

## 2.  Choose Your Tech Stack

| Category | Recommendation | Why |
|----------|----------------|-----|
| **Framework** | **Next.js** (React + SSR/SSG) | Built‑in routing, image optimisation, API routes, easy deployment on Vercel |
| **Language** | **TypeScript** | Compile‑time safety, better IDE support |
| **Styling** | **Tailwind CSS** + **Headless UI** | Rapid prototyping, utility‑first, fully responsive |
| **State** | **Zustand** (or Redux Toolkit) | Small bundle, simple API |
| **Data fetching** | **React Query** (or SWR) | Caching, background refetch, optimistic updates |
| **Component library** | **Storybook** | Isolated component development & documentation |
| **Testing** | **Jest + React Testing Library** | Unit & integration tests |
| **CI/CD** | **GitHub Actions** | Automate lint, test, build, deploy |
| **Hosting** | **Vercel** (or Netlify) | Zero‑config, instant preview, CDN |
| **Payments** | **Stripe** (or PayPal) | Secure, PCI‑compliant |
| **Auth** | **Auth0** or **Firebase Auth** | OAuth, social logins, MFA |
| **CMS** | **Sanity.io** or **Strapi** | Headless content for product descriptions, blogs, etc. |

> **Why Next.js?**  
> *SSR* gives you SEO out of the box.  
> *SSG* + *Incremental Static Regeneration* lets you pre‑render product pages and update them on demand.  
> *API Routes* let you keep business logic close to the UI without a separate backend.

---

